Description: thesaurus and dictionary for GNOME built on WordNet
 Onym is a thesaurus for GNOME. Look a word up and it shows the word's
 synonyms and antonyms, then the lexical relations that connect it to other
 words: what it is a kind of, its kinds, and the wholes and parts it belongs
 to, each as a tree you can open. Every word on screen is a link, so one
 lookup leads to the next with a click.
 .
 Each entry also carries its meanings, grouped by part of speech and shown
 with example sentences. Search is live, with completion as you type and a
 suggestion when a word is misspelt.
 .
 The word data comes from WordNet, the lexical database from Princeton
 University. The query engine is derived from Artha.
